Per-firing check (sea-vc --seam-check): every rule firing of the run
is a solver query `premise => lhs = rhs` on its terms (store-maps expanded);
an A-INB firing gets the layout and the in-bounds conditions of the accesses
the rule compares. On the SeaM programs every firing is valid, under z3 and
Yices, sampled or not. Under --simplify too.
RUN: sea-vc %S/store-map.mlir --lower --widen-memory=4 --seam --seam-check | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ALL
RUN: sea-vc %S/store-map-join.mlir --lower --widen-memory=4 --seam --seam-check | FileCheck %s
RUN: sea-vc %S/arm.mlir --lower --seam --seam-check | FileCheck %s
RUN: sea-vc %S/arm-inb-symbolic.mlir --lower --seam --seam-check | FileCheck %s
RUN: %if yices %{ sea-vc %S/join.mlir --lower --seam --seam-check --solver=yices | FileCheck %s %}
RUN: sea-vc %S/store-map-fork.mlir --lower --widen-memory=4 --seam --seam-check=5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAMPLE
RUN: sea-vc %S/nary-ops.mlir --lower --simplify --program=mul3m --seam-check | FileCheck %s
The check comes after the verdict and does not change a valid run's status.
ALL: result: unsat
ALL: seam-check: firings=[[N:[0-9]+]] checked=[[N]] valid=[[N]] invalid=0 unknown=0 unexpressible=0
CHECK: seam-check: firings=[[N:[0-9]+]] checked=[[N]] valid=[[N]] invalid=0 unknown=0 unexpressible=0
SAMPLE: seam-check: firings={{[0-9]+}} checked=5 valid=5 invalid=0 unknown=0 unexpressible=0

